## Quick plan (Amber)

```
What we are building: add a “Delete my account” button for logged‑in users.
Who uses it: existing users with personal data.  Risk level: Amber (logins + personal data).
Day‑one features: 1. Button on profile page. 2. Confirmation dialog. 3. Server‑side delete API.
Information it stores: yes – user data, files.
Logins: yes – only users can delete their own account.
Money: no payments involved.
Built with: Next.js API route + Supabase (Auth, Database, Storage).
Steps:
 1. Create API route /api/delete-account.js (server side).
 2. Add POST handler that deletes rows from tables where user_id matches.
 3. Delete files from the storage bucket whose metadata.user_id matches.
 4. Delete the Auth user via Supabase Admin API.
 5. Update the UI: put a “Delete my account” button, add confirmation, call the API.
 6. Add safety checks: only authenticated, confirm before deleting.
 7. Test locally, then deploy.  Save points before each step.
Safety: keys in .env only on server, data locked to user, confirm before act, 2‑step delete.
```

